  <!--
    MuJoCo analogue of the go2-wheel-toward training terrain at difficulty
    level 9 of 10 (difficulty 1.0 in tasks/wheel/terrain.py): a 4 x 4 array of
    flat tyres, outer radius 0.30 m, inner radius 0.20 m, centres 0.60 m apart,
    tyre heights fixed at 0.24 m. Each 0.10 m wide ring is
    approximated by 16 overlapping boxes whose tangential half-length
    0.059674 m = outer_radius * tan(pi / 16), so the hole and the
    vertical walls are preserved instead of using a solid disc.

    The array is centred at (2.7, 0), so the Go2 spawns at the origin facing
    +X exactly 1.5 m outside the near tyre edge, matching the training reset
    clearance (wheel_y = 2.7 = array half-extent 1.2 + 1.5 clearance) with the
    crossing direction along +X. The matching target is [5.4, 0.0].
  -->
